 "notes": "Document has 3 pages total. Page 3 is a signature/agreement page (\"Please review the following and sign in agreement...\") with no semester tables, so it was excluded per instructions.\n\nThis is an \"Accelerated Study Plan\" layout, not the standard 5-column major-map table. There is NO Min. Grade column, NO Code column, and NO Prerequisites column anywhere in the document \u2014 every row's min_grade, codes, and prerequisites is null. There is also no \"!\" critical-course marker system at all (no leftmost marker column exists in this bulleted layout), so critical=false for every row.\n\nThe document groups semesters under \"YEAR ONE\", \"YEAR TWO\", \"YEAR THREE\" headers (printed in red, larger type) that sit above the actual \"Fall Semester, X hours\" / \"Spring Semester, X hours\" / \"Summer Semester, X hours\" headers. The YEAR headers carry no rows or declared-credit total of their own \u2014 they are purely grouping labels \u2014 so I did not create separate section entries for them; only the Fall/Spring/Summer headers (which each have their own declared credit-hour total and a list of rows) were treated as sections, consistent with \"Only the semester tables.\"\n\nOne row is genuinely ambiguous: in Fall Semester (Year One), between the \"CHEM 111/111L (SCI), 4 hours\" row and the \"Foreign Language or Carolina Core, 3 hours\" row, the document prints an italicized parenthetical caveat on its own line: \"(Must have placed into MATH 111, 115, or higher MATH)\". It has no attached credit-hour value and appears to be a footnote-like qualifier on the MATH 122/141 row above it, but it is positioned lower in the print flow (likely a layout artifact). I transcribed it as its own row with credits=\"\" (empty string, since no value is printed and the schema requires a string) rather than merging it into the MATH row's title, since it is visually a separate paragraph/line. A parser could reasonably treat this differently (attach it to the MATH row, or drop it as a footnote) \u2014 flagging for review.\n\nIn Year Two Summer Semester, one row reads exactly \"Biological Sciences), 3 hours\" \u2014 a stray, unmatched closing parenthesis with no matching open parenthesis, transcribed verbatim per the no-fix-typos instruction. Also note: that section's 5 rows sum to 15 credit-hours, but its header declares \"12 hours\" \u2014 a real inconsistency in the source document (not a transcription artifact worth \"fixing\").\n\nNo total_credits_required is printed anywhere in the document (only per-semester hour totals appear), so that field is null. No department is named separately from the college, so department is null.",
